// PARAM: --analysis interval
// The conjunctive half of the branch gate, dual to
// 04-infeasible_disjunct_dropped.vimp. Concretely "y < 1" holds on the
// else-branch: x is 5, so "(x < 0) == 0" is true in every state, and the branch
// is taken only when the second conjunct is false.
//
// bfilter's "And _ _ False" case joins the two sides -- assuming the negation of
// a conjunction rules out one conjunct or the other -- and gates each side
// first. The first conjunct is infeasible for the assumed polarity, since it is
// definitely true, so that side contributes bot instead of its own unrefined
// incoming state and the join keeps what the second side established. Without
// the gate the first side would contribute y unconstrained: Interval's
// "inv_eq False" is the sound identity, so the Eq inversion narrows nothing,
// and the join would discard "y <= 0".
//
// The then-branch is the sequential "And _ _ True" case, where both conjuncts
// are narrowed in turn and no join is involved.
void main() {
  x := 5;
  y := __voblint_nondet_int();
  if ((x < 0) == 0 && 0 < y) {
    __voblint_check(0 < y) // PROVED
  } else {
    __voblint_check(y < 1) // PROVED
  }
}
